# novadeck linux-firmware pin — OPEN firmware blobs from the official linux-firmware
# repository, pinned by commit + per-file sha256 (the sha verifies the DOWNLOADED source).
#
# The upstream Holo aarch64 base ships NO /lib/firmware, so these `linux-fw`-class blobs
# (Adreno GPU, qca Wi-Fi/BT, Venus/Iris VPU, and on SM8250 the DSPs too) must be delivered
# by us. Blobs that are device-signed and absent upstream are NOT here — those come from
# the Nova-Deck/qcom-firmwares repo via firmware/fetch-qcom-fw.sh (firmware/QCOM_FW.pin).
# Which class a blob falls in is per-SoC, not fixed: the SM8550/SM8650 boards need
# vendor-signed adsp/cdsp, while every SM8250 board is served by the generic open pair.
#
# Columns:  <src-path-in-linux-firmware>  <install-path-under-/lib/firmware>  <sha256>
# '#' and blank lines are ignored. install-path may rename the file (e.g. the VPU signed
# variant) to the exact name the kernel driver requests.
#
# Fetch + verify with:  firmware/fetch-linux-fw.sh   (no arguments — one flat tree for
# every SoC; the unified Image embeds the union.)
# Pinned to a NAMED upstream release rather than a drive-by main commit, so the pin says what
# it is and a bump is reviewable. 20260810 is the tag; the commit below is that tag dereferenced
# (`git ls-remote '20260810^{}'`), because the plain/?id= endpoint wants a commit.
#
# Re-pinned 2026-08-18 from e7eb98afc667913acc533ab910c608bee7d08f25 (an untagged main commit)
# to the 20260810 release. Every one of the 23 rows below was re-downloaded at the new commit
# and hashed: ALL 23 are byte-identical, so not one sha changed. That is the expected result for
# a stable part -- these blobs only move when the vendor reships them -- and it is recorded here
# so the next bump does not read "no sha changed" as evidence the fetch silently no-op'd.
commit: 2135b2f7714a3a514c989b9728f51f36144cab6f
base:   https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/firmware/linux-firmware.git/plain

